{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful","id":1340611,"title":"What do you think of Princess: the Hopeful?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-10T06:34:03-07:00","id":1340611,"title":"What do you think of Princess: the Hopeful?","content":"Does it integrate well with the other Chronicles of Darkness games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T07:53:00-07:00","id":1340618,"title":"","content":"The best fanmade gameline next to Siren:The Drownings. Even if I don't integrate most of the time, I do make a reference here and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T11:03:17-07:00","id":1340646,"title":"","content":"I love it.! I never actually played any tabletop RPG but a like the Lore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T11:21:37-07:00","id":1340648,"title":"","content":"It's aight. It's one of the more solidly constructed fangames out there, with a lot of neat little hooks and evocative elements peppered throughout, enough to raise the more &quot;meh&quot; elements up with them. It sort of falls flat as a proper Chronicles-alike due to a number of dissonances regarding the ideas behind it's construction that keep it from meshing neatly with the feel of the rest of the world (the people who worked on it clearly didn't think of magical girls as monsters, it doesn't attempt to balance it's external horror with a sense of internal/personal horror, and while it clearly involves ambiguity and some things to question, at the core it's hard to maintain a mystery[a core feature and genre conceit of the rest of the setting] over a group of supernatural entities who you at least know at their core have their hearts pointed towards a &quot;general good&quot;, stuff like that), but it's definitely solid enough and does open a lot of interesting stories to tell, in isolation or conjoined with the rest of the Chronicles world. There's definitely fun to be had with playing it or using it in other games.<br /> <br /> I've got a personal soft spot for magical girls, so critical eye asides, I like it quite a fair bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T11:30:13-07:00","id":1340649,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> thanks. I'll defo have to check it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T10:31:42-07:00","id":1341276,"title":"","content":"love princess Think its well written not sure how well it integrates though<br /> <br /> <br /> it was Princess though that got me into Nwod/Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> One thing I've been wonder recently though? <br /> <br /> What happens when a DarkSpawn has a Umbra or Caligio that depends on conscious thought or use? Like that makes you a gifted liar or lockpick","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T12:01:49-07:00","id":1341292,"title":"","content":"@princeofthenight wow! You've got a lot of badges.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't know the answer to your question, but I think having an Umbra that makes you a gifted liar would be very useful for a more socially-oriented DarkSpawn.<br /> <br /> \u200bJust a thought. I wonder if the Contagion from the Contagion Chronicle could be tied into the Darkness in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T12:04:12-07:00","id":1341294,"title":"","content":"Considering the Contagion is actually a series of contagions that can be created in accordance to your game, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T13:31:23-07:00","id":1341312,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I only read one small part of the Contagion Chronicle preview, but that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T14:01:25-07:00","id":1341320,"title":"","content":"From what I've seen the Darkness is a very dull and generic villain, it's history is very oWoD with the origin of princesses returning straight up being from &quot;Changeling the Dreaming&quot;, and the power set is sort of bloated, and the tone doesn't feel very Chronicles of Darkness to me. I know some like it, but I'm personally not a big fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T14:45:49-07:00","id":1341324,"title":"","content":"What if you replaced the Darkness with the Dark One (Lucifer) from Second Sight and Inferno? You could do kind of like a feminist take on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T15:05:59-07:00","id":1341325,"title":"","content":"I enjoy it. For me the straight up &quot;Good vs Evil&quot; feel of it actually is something I can live with in CoD since it's such a great contrast to the other gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T20:28:19-07:00","id":1341387,"title":"","content":"what about the Caligae &quot;Copycat Crime&quot;? and a few others<br /> <br /> think the Darkspawn are capable of this much strategy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T20:50:40-07:00","id":1341393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1341276#post1341276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">love princess Think its well written not sure how well it integrates though<br /> <br /> <br /> it was Princess though that got me into Nwod/Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> One thing I've been wonder recently though?<br /> <br /> What happens when a DarkSpawn has a Umbra or Caligio that depends on conscious thought or use? Like that makes you a gifted liar or lockpick</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Darkspawn are have a certain cunning. For example, the lockpick I would give to a goblin or gremlin like Darkspawn that liked to go into places and smash up machines. A gifted liar could be used for a darkspawn that's like a Psycho scourage or a L4D Witch - they can feign humanity well enough to get you to let your guard down.<br /> <br /> Aside from the two openly destructive Twilight Courts, (Tear's hope draining and Storms 'burn the world to save the world' mentality), Princesses can be anti-heroic monsters. There's Mirrors from an outsider's point of view, rather than being a narcisstic, arrogant jerk, could be seen as brainwashing people into their cult of sorts. There's also a fan-made (but widely accepted, fan works have a solid acceptance in the PtH community) hunter supplement, and for various reasons, hunters have varying views. TFV, for example, sees Princesses as supernatural vigilantees at best, at worst agents of a foreign monarchy. Union may see potential allies to protect the neighborhood, or draw guns at the first sight of them because they had to clean up after a Tear's hope raid. Long Night could see them as gifts from heaven or as a particularly deluded type of witch. And even a Radiant might get on a Hunter's bad side when they break into their safe place to rescue a friend.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri","name":"Tzauri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T09:30:14-07:00","id":1341459,"title":"","content":"looked at hunters<br /> <br /> <br /> By as agents of a foreign monarchy<br /> <br /> <br /> Imagine how TFV Would feel if they learned of the reality of reincarnation?<br /> <br /> That princesses could be born into any of the US's first families<br /> <br /> basicly infiltrating them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T11:52:38-07:00","id":1342771,"title":"","content":"Random followup question<br /> <br /> \u200bIf I run a Princess game, should I put the Dreamlands in the Oneiros or the Temenos? Or doesn't it make a difference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T12:47:10-07:00","id":1342778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1342771#post1342771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random followup question<br /> <br /> \u200bIf I run a Princess game, should I put the Dreamlands in the Oneiros or the Temenos? Or doesn't it make a difference?</div> </div> </div> </div>Temenos. Oneiros are individual soul spaces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T13:13:22-07:00","id":1342790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1342771#post1342771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random followup question<br /> <br /> \u200bIf I run a Princess game, should I put the Dreamlands in the Oneiros or the Temenos? Or doesn't it make a difference?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Oneiros is the individual soul, the Temenos is the shared soul of humanity, so probably the latter.<br /> <br /> [Edit]The Primordial Dream from Beast is also in the Temenos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 10-21-2019, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T16:09:58-07:00","id":1342824,"title":"","content":"Thanks. That works perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T17:32:26-07:00","id":1342838,"title":"","content":"Curious for my own princess game Im putting together<br /> <br /> Think a Darkspawn<br /> <br /> Darkened<br /> <br /> Mneosmye or Cataphract is better?<br /> <br /> For someone who uses &quot;Copycat Crime&quot; to create a tainted place?<br /> <br /> in a small one horse town that is currently relatively free of taint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-21-2019, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T15:15:42-07:00","id":1343026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1341320#post1341320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've seen the Darkness is a very dull and generic villain, it's history is very oWoD with the origin of princesses returning straight up being from &amp;quot;Changeling the Dreaming&amp;quot;, and the power set is sort of bloated, and the tone doesn't feel very Chronicles of Darkness to me. I know some like it, but I'm personally not a big fan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I don\u2019t like the whole \u2018The Moon landing\u201d was one of the most inspirational and spiritual uplifting event ever, maybe because I wasn\u2019t born there, even then it seems really Eurocentric.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T16:39:30-07:00","id":1343042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1343026#post1343026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I don\u2019t like the whole \u2018The Moon landing\u201d was one of the most inspirational and spiritual uplifting event ever, maybe because I wasn\u2019t born there, even then it seems really Eurocentric.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know there's a big ocean between the country that landed astronauts on the Moon and the continent of Europe, right?<br /> <br /> Amerocentric, sure, but Eurocentric?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T16:52:52-07:00","id":1343045,"title":"","content":"Eurocentric should probably have said Western centric but that doesn\u2019t roll of the tongue, what about the first men in space Yuri gangan,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T18:32:58-07:00","id":1343067,"title":"","content":"I understand there are two versions of this: a Vocation version and a Dream version. How do they differ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-22-2019, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T19:46:12-07:00","id":1343080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1343067#post1343067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand there are two versions of this: a Vocation version and a Dream version. How do they differ?</div> </div> </div> </div>One way I've heard it put.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#DCDDDE\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dream envisions Princesses as deeply connected to mundane society, and is envisioned as a toolbox that can create any magical girl story (at least in theme and styles) and could be used for a something like Magical Angel Creamy Mami as easily as a something like Sailor Nothing. Vocation envisions the Princesses as more connected to supernatural society, and is also supposed to be a game for war stories, with even combat-free games being set against the backdrop of the War of Hope and resembling something like M</span></span></span><i>A</i><span style=\"color:#DCDDDE\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">S*H.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Granted, this isn't SUPER the case. You could easily play either in either. The system is fairly similar, and you could easily important charms from one to the other, for instance. Vocation has a mechanic that allows you to create a nation, which is a light-ran organization. At high end, even mundanes can start using light magic. Dreams figures Nobles tend to use mundane organizations.<br /> <br /> There's some different charms, though there's a lot of overlap. IMO, from a combat perspective, Dreams has defensive emplacements, and has Athletics-based ranged weapons (Javelot) as different from their firearms (Levinbolts) while Vocation merges the two, just pick your stat. Vocation also has magical shields (as in, swords and shields). Vocation has some charms that let you directly apply an invocation trait to a given skill's roll (and for just 1 XP each, presuming affinity), while Dreams prefers supporting skills with other means. Last, part of the cost of Lacrima charms in Dreams are 'breaking point if at or above Belief X' while it's sensativity rolls in Vocation.<br /> <br /> Aside from those though, the two versions are pretty similar. It's kinda a touchy subject in PtH circles which is better, but they're pretty close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri","name":"Tzauri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T04:28:57-07:00","id":1343122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1340648#post1340648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">keep it from meshing neatly with the feel of the rest of the world (the people who worked on it clearly didn't think of magical girls as monsters</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the same can be said of mages and sin eaters, the latter of which are glorified even more than nobles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T08:50:00-07:00","id":1343189,"title":"","content":"I think magical girls are cool. They're like a counterpoint to the darkness of the rest of the CoD universe. And when a Princess falls for a hot Daeva...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T10:40:07-07:00","id":1343210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1343122#post1343122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, the same can be said of mages and sin eaters, the latter of which are glorified even more than nobles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noooooope. Dave Brookshaw has gone out of his was to make mages monsters (and succeeded), and while Sin-Eaters are given a (very nice) heavy branding of Social Justice Necromancers, conversations with Vera on while I was working on Memento Mori made it clear that everyone's given the directions to keep the Bound monsters, and that that followed from Travis Stout's direction.<br /> <br /> I'll leave it at that-if we wanna do this song and dance (<i>again</i>), you can make another thread about it.<br /> <br /> As it concerns this one though, I know for a <i>fact</i> though that None of the people claiming Developer status over Princess wanted to portray magical girls as monsters, and some didn't even think of that as a question. (I'm a sucker for development logs)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T10:47:26-07:00","id":1343213,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> I'm really glad to hear it. Your last paragraph, I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T11:25:46-07:00","id":1343225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1343213#post1343213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> I'm really glad to hear it. Your last paragraph, I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>To each their own-like I said, Princess ain't a bad game, but it is tonally and thematically dissonant with the rest of the Chronicles world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T13:09:38-07:00","id":1343254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1343210#post1343210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noooooope. Dave Brookshaw has gone out of his was to make mages monsters (and succeeded), and while Sin-Eaters are given a (very nice) heavy branding of Social Justice Necromancers, conversations with Vera on while I was working on Memento Mori made it clear that everyone's given the directions to keep the Bound monsters, and that that followed from Travis Stout's direction.<br /> <br /> I'll leave it at that-if we wanna do this song and dance (<i>again</i>), you can make another thread about it.<br /> <br /> As it concerns this one though, I know for a <i>fact</i> though that None of the people claiming Developer status over Princess wanted to portray magical girls as monsters, and some didn't even think of that as a question. (I'm a sucker for development logs)</div> </div> </div> </div>What does that mean \u201cMages where made monsters\u201d the first edition books had them seem like prideful Hubristic Jerks,<br /> <br /> And what is monstrous about Sin-eaters they are Social justice necromancers <br /> <br /> I heard they where both retold cause playing them could get out of focus!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T13:16:25-07:00","id":1343258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1343254#post1343254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What does that mean \u201cMages where made monsters\u201d the first edition books had them seem like prideful Hubristic Jerks,<br /> <br /> And what is monstrous about Sin-eaters they are Social justice necromancers<br /> <br /> I heard they where both retold cause playing them could get out of focus!</div> </div> </div> </div>I know people have talked to you about Mages before, and there are also whole threads on the subject. I'll dig up the pertinents later.(Edit: Here's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/830278-mages-as-monsters\">a whole thread</a> on the subject that also has some great dick jokes.) (Edit: And if you want a brief treatiese on how Mages are monsters if your definition of monsters is Villain, I recall <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1311715#post1311715\">this conversation</a>.)<br /> <br /> And Sin-Eaters are monsters who happen to be Social Justice Necromancers. They are still ghosts, with a drive to haunt the living for their own ends. Nothing about the Bargain and the quirks of their bodies as part of that package or the politics of their death religions changes that.<br /> <br /> There are several definitions of monster, most of which have no concern over the morality or ethics of the entities in question. Of course, a good many do (Hi Hunters, you're monsters too!)<br /> <br /> Again, if we wanna make a thing out of this, someone start a new thread on it, we're distracting from Princess here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-23-2019, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T14:29:59-07:00","id":1343275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1343258#post1343258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know people have talked to you about Mages before, and there are also whole threads on the subject. I'll dig up the pertinents later.(Edit: Here's <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/830278-mages-as-monsters&amp;quot;]a</a> whole thread[/URL] on the subject that also has some great dick jokes.) (Edit: And if you want a brief treatiese on how Mages are monsters if your definition of monsters is Villain, I recall <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1311715#post1311715&amp;quot;]this</a> conversation[/URL].)<br /> <br /> And Sin-Eaters are monsters who happen to be Social Justice Necromancers. They are still ghosts, with a drive to haunt the living for their own ends. Nothing about the Bargain and the quirks of their bodies as part of that package or the politics of their death religions changes that.<br /> <br /> There are several definitions of monster, most of which have no concern over the morality or ethics of the entities in question. Of course, a good many do (Hi Hunters, you're monsters too!)<br /> <br /> Again, if we wanna make a thing out of this, someone start a new thread on it, we're distracting from Princess here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I remember reading the Mage books and getting a weird \u201cthe Magic\u2019s mans burden\u201d thing. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m actually thinking of a Mage character who is/was a Disability/minority Activist (doesn\u2019t have hands)and clashes with the colonialist/ ableist shit in mage Society,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T15:24:18-07:00","id":1343287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1343258#post1343258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, if we wanna make a thing out of this, someone start a new thread on it, we're distracting from Princess here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but you brought it up as a way to snipe against Princess and claim that it doesn't fit with the rest of the CofD.<br /> <br /> Either way, &quot;mediums&quot; and &quot;mages,&quot; neither of which have to pay for their status through monstrous acts, pacts with evil beings, and so on, are more in the genre of magical girls than protagonists-as-monsters. The only difference is that mages sometimes choose to act like jerks (despite that there's nothing more jerkish about mana-aspirations than vanilla-aspirations), which is fine; far more nobles act in a jerkish fashion than mages, as for the bulk of human history, the only representatives of nobles has been the Twilight Court.<br /> <br /> Its fine that some fan games are in the &quot;power with responsibilities but no actual requirement to be a monster&quot; category, since two big time CofD games are in that category too.<br /> <br /> I don't buy dead people are intrinsically monsters and I doubt you could find anything in Sin Eater implying that they are. That's just not part of SE's themes or branding. But if ghosts are somehow monsters, then hey, the only long term noble civilization is pretty monstery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T15:54:00-07:00","id":1343293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1343287#post1343287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but you brought it up as a way to snipe against Princess and claim that it doesn't fit with the rest of the CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had it as a sidenote that is largely unimportant to the main thrust of the conversation and other people decided they wanted to confront me about it. In fact, it was <i>literally you</i> who decided to make an issue out of it.<br /> <br /> As it relates to Princess, if we must go through this, then<br /> <br /> The Chronicles of Darkness is a game fundamentally about monsters and using the various ways in which their splats are monsters as a means of looking at people and the world for it's humanist (and other) themes and ideas-to this end, every splat must account for the fact that it's entity is a monster and answer How That Is, Why That Is, and What The Implies. Internal, personal horror is an extension of that, that there are things about the way the various splats view things or interact with the world or experience it that belies the monstrous nature, that enforces an angle of alienation. Predacity is also a significant force and metaphor at work within any of the splat, a temptation if not a neccesity that invariably works it's way in, that people will &quot;eat&quot; one another given the right or wrong set of circumstances. Chronicles is also a game of dark mystery, where in the main form of darkness is not predicated on &quot;evil&quot;, &quot;immoral&quot;, &quot;unethical&quot;, or &quot;squicky&quot; but upon <i>uncertainty</i>, upon information not being clear, with true intentions being murky, with being, well, <i>mysterious. </i>Every other gameline engages in the splat type as monster, how that works, how they may prey upon others, and the mystery and hard decisions of the game.<br /> <br /> Princess the Hopeful is a game that predicated on it's main source of horror being external, that it's not the condition of being a magical girl that is where it's horror comes from, but from the atrocity and despair that surrounds them. While minor elements feed into the theme of predacity and what drives people to commiting acts of it, by and large the Nobility doesn't really <i>predate</i> on others, even in their darkest hours without popping over into the villain groups. Nothing about it used either as a monster or in that way the Monster-As-Lens idea is used within the rest of the canon. They also fundamentally dodge the dark mystery theme and genre because, while every noble is fundmentally different and have their own angle on things, it's hard to feel the dread uncertainty so important for the setting when every Noble is essentially aligned to a metaphysical force of Unapologetic, Indisputable Good.<br /> <br /> It does not fit in with the rest of the Chronicles worlds on this tonal and thematic level-and honestly, a Lot of people love it For That Reason. I like it In Spite of That, leaning on everything else that it does well. It's not a problem, it is simply a thing to note for people who may be looking for certain things.<br /> <br /> Now if you want to keep arguing about Mages and Sin-Eaters, <i>make another fucking thread for it already.</i> Otherwise, stop wasting our time and distracting from the thread's focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-02-2020, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T20:07:16-07:00","id":1343331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1343293#post1343293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Princess the Hopeful is a game that predicated on it's main source of horror being external, that it's not the condition of being a magical girl that is where it's horror comes from, but from the atrocity and despair that surrounds them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like SE, whose themes don't include &quot;predation&quot; and &quot;personal horror&quot; but rather empathy, hope and joy, and self vs service. And yeah, you were the one who compared Princess to the rest of CofD, so I don't see why seeing whether PtH is on par with, at a minimum, Mage and SE is off topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T20:12:46-07:00","id":1343332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1343331#post1343331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like SE, whose themes don't include &quot;predation&quot; and &quot;personal horror&quot; but rather empathy, hope and joy, and self vs service. And yeah, you were the one who compared Princess to the rest of CofD, so I don't see why seeing whether PtH is on par with, at a minimum, Mage and SE is off topic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> just stop. You are the one that brought up Mages and Sin-Eaters. Do not shift the blame and let's just return to talking about Princess. I could talk about why Sin-eaters are monsters myself, but I really don't want to in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 10-23-2019, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T21:51:44-07:00","id":1343344,"title":"","content":"One thing in the PDF it talks about Bestial darkspawn so their must be some nonbestial ones...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T22:23:35-07:00","id":1343348,"title":"","content":"That has been discussed by people I know. they probably exist, but you don't need any special rules to run them. They just are Darkspawn that can talk and plan and maybe use human tools if they still or ever had hands with a humanoid precision grip capability. They're just as cruel and hungry and totally evil. Biggest difference is probably that they use lowest of Wits or Dexterity instead of higher stat like their animalistic counterparts<br /> <br /> Edit: there is a semi-sentient Darkspawn example character in the book too. She's the one who acts as a caretaker/maid to the wheel-chair bound mnemosyne. She's also his emergency muscle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 10-24-2019, 01:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T02:22:39-07:00","id":1343363,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> I don\u2019t entirely understand a lot of what you wrote, but I agree completely with the last sentence of the fourth paragraph. If I ever ran Princess (which I probably won\u2019t; I\u2019ve never run a game, just played in them), I would make it a little more morally ambiguous. Less 100% straight good versus straight evil. Even D&amp;D (usually) isn\u2019t like that. I like games that explore shades of grey. I just like magical girls too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T12:32:59-07:00","id":1343482,"title":"","content":"Poorly-written, badly-constructed cringefest completely out of sync with the general tone of CofD. In other words, one of the better fansplats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T12:43:13-07:00","id":1343486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1343482#post1343482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poorly-written, badly-constructed cringefest completely out of sync with the general tone of CofD. In other words, one of the better fansplats.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not bad in either it's writing or construction, though it definitely shows it's seams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T13:43:56-07:00","id":1343491,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25584_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25584\" data-vbnamecard=\"25584\">Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</a> I loved it. I thought it was a great counterpoint to the rest of the Chronicles of Darkness universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T17:44:56-07:00","id":1343522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1343482#post1343482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poorly-written, badly-constructed cringefest completely out of sync with the general tone of CofD. In other words, one of the better fansplats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you say that? I liked it,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-24T22:53:13-07:00","id":1343540,"title":"","content":"I like Princess quite a lot. I know there's dedicated systems out there to play anime-style games, but I'm not familiar with those. I'm a horror fan who's an incidental anime fan, and an incidental anime fan who's an even more incidental magical girl fan. Princess took a genre I thought was neat and made it accessible to me by tying it to a setting and game system I was more familiar with.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I'd have a hard time integrating Princess into most CofD games. (And this is speaking as someone who's run part of a game in all-girls high school...) It's not the themes so much as it is the feel. I frankly could not drop something like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-F2KhA1Y1Dk\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> into a session with a straight face. My players would all start laughing. And I'd laugh along with them. It's just too out of whack with the larger setting's atmosphere. <br /> <br /> I guess you could swap out a princess' transformation and other &quot;cosmetic&quot; elements of the game for something lower-key. But I think you risk throwing out the baby with the bathwater by making it low-key enough for the CofD. The sparkles and flashy effects, the pimped-out dresses, the cutesy factor, the whole premise of innocent young waifs with superpowers... it's sort of the point of the genre. Taking that away feels like trying to fit a square peg into a round hole. <br /> <br /> Then again, I haven't watched/read all that many magical girl stories. Maybe it is possible to do a magical girl story with an ambiance that's less sugar-sweet, more grimdark, and all-around lower-key. I'm not sure how that would look, though. Puella Magi Madoka was a pretty grimdark and deconstructionist take on the genre, and it still has a lot of cosmetic magical girl trappings that would feel out of place to me in the CofD. The kawaii-looking companion critter might actually be a ruthless cannibal, but even a superficially kawaii critter doesn't have a place in the setting I prefer. <br /> <br /> Next to revising the game's atmosphere, tweaking its themes is easy. Get rid of the queens as all-powerful forces of cosmic good in favor of a setup like Puella's. Have the girls empowered by a force with more ambiguous and potentially sinister motives, and make unraveling its purpose a bigger element of the game. Turn the &quot;bad&quot; queens into ascended princesses who've cut their ties to that force and argue their way is the only way to make a lasting difference in the world.<br /> <br /> Heck, that setup actually interests me more than 2e Geist's &quot;sin-eater social activists fighting the good fight against the 1%&quot; does. 1e Geist lacked a clear purpose and direction for sin-eaters, but turning them into one of the closest things the CofD has to a good guy faction bored me to tears. At least hunters had PC-inclusive factions like Ashwood Abbey and the Cheiron Group who upheld the Vigil for purely dickish reasons.<br /> <br /> Princesses being turned into monsters by external rather than internal forces is an interesting point, but I think the CofD has room and precedent for more thematically divergent splats. Beast celebrates being the PCs being monsters rather than making feel bad for it, down to having no Integrity-equivalent stat. Granted, I also didn't like Beast, so gamelines with bigger thematic divergences are less likely to appeal to as many fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T04:15:50-07:00","id":1343556,"title":"","content":"@FalseEpiphany if I ever ran Princess, I would do it with a little more moral ambiguity and a little more emphasis on romance and sexuality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T04:16:23-07:00","id":1343557,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3110_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3110\" data-vbnamecard=\"3110\">False Epiphany</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T14:16:31-07:00","id":1343651,"title":"","content":"I thing the Darkness kind of boring to. You could use other Antagonists. Like in Mage\u2019s Abyss Book there is a Bloodline that Carries the Abyss In them and the PC\u2019s have a ethical dilemma of murdering innocent people. Cause they carry the abyss in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T14:21:58-07:00","id":1343656,"title":"","content":"(I\u2019m sorry; I can\u2019t spell your name)<br /> <br /> What about conflating the Darkness with Lucifer the Dark One? By giving the Darkness a gender, you give the Princesses a tangible symbol of oppression to fight against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-25T19:31:07-07:00","id":1343703,"title":"","content":"One thing I find brilliant about PtH is that while, like most CofD settings, it has a force of relentless evil, that this force is not unbeatable and is usually something the protagonists can overcome. Its similar to beasts with heroes in that respect; the protags are not outclassed and are not up against unstoppable deities. Geist is similar, though reapers can get big dice pools.<br /> <br /> Only thing I don't really like is Belief, I find the notion of oft-younger protagonists being locked into rigidity of thought or else they will suffer mental decay to be highly depressing, since your younger years are usually the time set aside, in humans, for it to be okay to have stupid beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T04:59:58-07:00","id":1343962,"title":"","content":"I agree with you about belief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-10T19:06:11-08:00","id":1347598,"title":"","content":"Oh a curious Question? Is a dark creature immune to social Maneuvering? <br /> <br /> Was thinking if it isn't it would let a grace be a part of trying to resolve a tainted place by Convincing Emanations of various things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T02:21:46-08:00","id":1347644,"title":"","content":"I think social maneuvering would be a major weapon in a Princess\u2019s arsenal, so no, I don\u2019t think creatures of the Dark should be immune to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T03:09:25-08:00","id":1347647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1347644#post1347644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think social maneuvering would be a major weapon in a Princess\u2019s arsenal, so no, I don\u2019t think creatures of the Dark should be immune to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends. Darkspawn aren't sapient, and are basically very evil inclined animals. Memosyme are incapable of being decent people because they are a person shaped shell of cosmic evil. Dethroned can be &quot;reasoned&quot; with, but it involes letting them hitch a ride on your soul so you can get them some therapy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"