rid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T20:13:34-08:00","id":1349762,"title":"","content":"the rules need edited in some cases.<br /> <br /> In some cases BADLY<br /> <br /> On the hunters and Social maneuvering thing for some reason I'd like it to take multiple encounters to get them to give up their Insane crusade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T21:11:00-08:00","id":1349774,"title":"","content":"I'm actually one of the originators of the Cataphractoi idea; I think I'm the one who suggested they should be revenants. <br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of a Night Horrors book for them, but also thinking about a Princess/Mummy 2E Contagion strain based on Lypothymie, from Exalted; a transmissible nostalgia that causes people to lose themselves in imagined glories of what the Kindgom and Irem were... which make them perfect prey for people who want to turn them into revanchist fanatics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T02:53:13-08:00","id":1349824,"title":"","content":"oh curious is a Cataphract or Mneosmye a better breed for exploring<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MightAsWellNotBeInPrisonAtAll\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p...eInPrisonAtAll</a><br /> <br /> Thinking he went through transformation already in a life sentence<br /> <br /> And is acting as a General of the Darkness unseen by the princesses as of yet.<br /> <br /> And maybe has made Dolls of guards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T05:10:13-08:00","id":1349843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1349774#post1349774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually one of the originators of the Cataphractoi idea; I think I'm the one who suggested they should be revenants. <br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of a Night Horrors book for them, but also thinking about a Princess/Mummy 2E Contagion strain based on Lypothymie, from Exalted; a transmissible nostalgia that causes people to lose themselves in imagined glories of what the Kindgom and Irem were... which make them perfect prey for people who want to turn them into revanchist fanatics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that\u2019s cool. We talked about this on Discord. I\u2019m thinking of a Noble that ostensibly Is the Reincarnation of one of the Monarchs from a lost Kingdom of Light. Who\u2019s Kingdom suffers greatly under Darkness and then.Who was trapped in the Darkness. Escaped and went to the Great Wheel. There newest Reincarnation is understandable Traumatized by the whole thing. And is willing to do Morally compromising things. \u201cNot sure about the specifics.\u201d<br /> <br /> Maybe they could have been under the \u201cCare\u201d of the Darkness Cult Asylum.<br /> <br /> I think it could add to you social commentary. And have her by a AIM activist, that was sent to a insane asylum cause she is thought to by \u201cInsane\u201d for questioning the capitalist status quo.<br /> <br /> See this <a href=\"https://r.search.yahoo.com/_ylt=A0geKeU6OdVdg0oAFHnBGOd_;_ylu=X3oDMTEyZG9laDZ2BGNvbG8DYmYxBHBvcwMxBHZ0aWQDQjY1NDdfMQRzZWMDc3I-/RV=2/RE=1574283706/RO=10/RU=https%3a%2f%2fnewsmaven.io%2findiancountrytoday%2farchive%2fa-living-burial-inside-the-hiawatha-asylum-for-insane-indians-7NZ2CDyrf02QuQZxUZBKgg%2f/RK=2/RS=NHK94K53gDOYILHYyKvKTVZ4Pks-\" target=\"_blank\">https://r.search.yahoo.com/_ylt=A0ge...HYyKvKTVZ4Pks-</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T17:59:55-08:00","id":1349960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1349744#post1349744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Got a link? Google gives a lot of different results, none of which reference CofD 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>The PDFs themselves say &quot;Princess: the Hopeful is a fan-made roleplaying game for the Chronicles of Darkness, published by White Wolf Publishing. The Chronicles of Darkness book is needed to use this book.&quot; They haven't pointed to the GMC since the 2e corebook was published.<br /> <br /> And if you go to the Google Sites page, you'll get the most recent versions of both PDFs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T22:34:35-08:00","id":1350392,"title":"","content":"Is it legitimate for a Cataphraph mneosmye or Dethroned to recognize that a Darkened is sufficiently Valuable as a Darkened to slow the Transformation to a Darkspawn<br /> <br /> <br /> Is keeping him out of stressful situations the best way to do so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T09:20:38-08:00","id":1351056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1347697#post1347697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13566_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13566\" data-vbnamecard=\"13566\">Kalzky</a> do you like the idea that Princesses are 100% sweetness and light and the Darkness is 100% evil? Do you think there should be grey areas?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Here's the thing. Princesses may be intended to be 100% sweetness and light, but they aren't. Look at the stereotype sections (at least in the version for the 2e rules). They come off as completely judgmental jerks bordering on murderous jerks. There's one who that asks mages why they aren't curing cancer ignoring that not all mages can. And pretty universally, their Beast ones indicate they're one &quot;justification&quot; away from ethnic cleansing because of their need to feed on fear (though oddly the splat that chooses to feed on Fear seems to get a pass).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6356-vernuf","name":"vernuf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T10:57:23-08:00","id":1351072,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6356-vernuf\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6356\" data-vbnamecard=\"6356\">vernuf</a> I agree with you. There's definitely an elitist attitude among certain Noble cliques (especially in the Twilight Courts, but to some extent in the Courts of Light as well, especially with Hearts and Diamonds). A certain sense of <i>noblesse oblige</i>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T02:43:19-08:00","id":1351817,"title":"","content":"The Peoples Guard go way too far but they are kind of onto something.<br /> <br /> <br /> Kinda sorta...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T21:08:52-08:00","id":1353240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KnightFenrirWulfhart</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1348154#post1348154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all honesty P:tH is a great standalone game, I adore it. But as a crossover game its not very good because P:tH either will completely overshadow everything else which is fine just be straight up about it, and it has no reason why they should not be using charms all over the place in big flashy ways.<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> I, personally, feel a Noble should derive their inner power not from the objective good vs evil but from how much they believe in their cause.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is an example of how they overshadow others?<br /> <br /> Also, your beliefs already have a huge emphasis on your behavior. I have not remotely heard of a crossover chronicle in which the princesses acted too &quot;perfectly,&quot; more often I hear about them taking really stupid, extreme ideologies and cranking them up to 11.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T00:12:17-08:00","id":1353268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1353240#post1353240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is an example of how they overshadow others?<br /> <br /> Also, your beliefs already have a huge emphasis on your behavior. I have not remotely heard of a crossover chronicle in which the princesses acted too &amp;quot;perfectly,&amp;quot; more often I hear about them taking really stupid, extreme ideologies and cranking them up to 11.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Noble's charms are pretty powerful in a lot of different fields with very little drawbacks from what I remember. They don't have any real reason to not go all out with their charms as much as their wisp stores allow. <br /> But the real reason they overshadow the other lines is that Nobles pretty much imply by their existence that there is objective good and objective evil and they can pretty much fuck up any other splats shit much easier than the other splats could with them. (From what I remember. I havent read the books in a while so I might be misremembering some things in which case- apologies!)<br /> As with all things this isn't to say that they wouldn't be fun to play with other splats, in fact with some tweaks and some unique concepts for characters and less moral absolutism Nobles would be beautiful monsters of &quot;good.&quot; <br /> I don't like any mechanics that tell you you're character is (in a way) weaker if they don't have a perfect set of subjective morals. So that definitely makes me biased so I won't even argue that. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T01:25:23-08:00","id":1353505,"title":"","content":"I see. I've always thought of nobles as on the weak end of things, with overspecialized charms that aren't any stronger for their narrowness. Look at Kensai vs a deviant's Lash or a vampire's Claws of the Unholy for example. Having better &quot;subjective morals&quot; giving you advantage isn't a new thing, though, look at Humanity or Wisdom. [cue series of complaints about how those aren't morality stats]<br /> <br /> I don't see any problem with nobles coming into conflict with other protagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T05:35:11-08:00","id":1353530,"title":"","content":"In dream at least charms are a point thing. buy a dot in Inspire and you get all the charms that use one dot in inspire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T15:17:47-08:00","id":1354678,"title":"","content":"That's not true Konradleijon. That's a houserule we discussed on the forums that you could use if you were playing a Noble in a Mage-focused game","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T06:56:47-08:00","id":1354993,"title":"","content":"on the hunters Supplement an idea I had is a another group in stars of bethlahem one focused on people they see as 'enablers' but I think theyd be small and all their methods still experimental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T18:06:48-08:00","id":1358316,"title":"","content":"I like the Magic Girl;(Magic Boy), concept. <br /> <br /> I can definitely see them as part of Mage. I once read an online article about how the whole Magic Girl concept is based on stories of Japanese Witches. Unfortunately I didn't have the presence of mind to print out the article when I read it and now the site no longer exists. <br /> <br /> I can see the Magic Girls as Changelings. Perhaps as unwitting pawns of some fey lord.<br /> <br /> I can see Magic Girls as Hunters. Particularly Hunters that specialize in going after Beasts.<br /> <br /> Deviant Magic girls could be the product of some government or multinational corporation.<br /> <br /> I don't see them fitting into any other storyline except as antagonists, though I suppose Geist Magic Girls might be possible.<br /> <br /> I think Princess works best as a supplement or even as a chronicle for the existing game lines.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-02T11:48:20-08:00","id":1358457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwolf8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1358316#post1358316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can definitely see them as part of Mage. I once read an online article about how the whole Magic Girl concept is based on stories of Japanese Witches. Unfortunately I didn't have the presence of mind to print out the article when I read it and now the site no longer exists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The magical girl concept first came from the anime <i>Sally the Witch</i>, which was inspired by the American sticom <i>Bewitched</i>. Originally the only magical girl anime were of the &quot;cute witch&quot; variety, it wasn't until a few years later that the &quot;magical girl warrior&quot; came along, and iirc it wasn't until <i>Sailor Moon</i> that magical girl warrior eclipsed cute witch for the magical girl genre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T22:07:19-08:00","id":1367395,"title":"","content":"Curious any ideas how a school aged hopeful can Go about performing Consecrate on Campus getting the Ritual behavior overlooked to Consecrate the School or part of it so its free from darkspawn attacks and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T05:00:50-08:00","id":1367491,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1153\" data-vbnamecard=\"1153\">Prince of the Night</a> Pretend your character is a Wiccan and Consecrate is a religious ritual protected by the First Amendment. This would work especially well at a private school where the characters live on campus anyway.<br /> <br /> Let me ask you a question. Would a male Prince be different from a female Princess in some basic way (other than not being susceptible to the charms of Prince Charming), or is gender basically irrelevant to the Hopeful when it comes to their mission of protecting people from the Darkness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T06:58:11-08:00","id":1367523,"title":"","content":"They use separate terms sometimes for Male princes.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T07:15:22-08:00","id":1367527,"title":"","content":"I know. Would they solve problems differently? Would they experience emotions differently? Would a Prince of Hearts and a Princess of Hearts react to a romantic crisis (or an issue with the Darkness) differently? Or do you think it depends more on the individual Prince or Princess's personality and not so much on their gender?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T09:37:24-08:00","id":1367551,"title":"","content":"probably the last<br /> <br /> Oh curious thing?<br /> <br /> does a princess with a transformed identity opposite her mundane gender need to be Transgendered.<br /> <br /> or think it would be possible for her to dress and act normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-13T10:12:50-08:00","id":1367558,"title":"","content":"I don't think a Princess whose Royal identity and mundane identity are different genders necessarily needs to be transgendered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T10:17:02-08:00","id":1368965,"title":"","content":"One odd thing on the Hunters? <br /> <br /> Peoples Guard MURDERS Nobles<br /> <br /> Magisters just send them into Coma's.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on Why I find it easier to picture any Noble I played Showing Forgiveness and Mercy to a member of the Peoples guard then a Magister<br /> <br /> or is it just me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T10:28:22-08:00","id":1368968,"title":"","content":"If you're talking to me, you'll have to remind me who the People's Guard and the Magisters are. Been a while since I read the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T16:27:57-08:00","id":1369048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1368965#post1368965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One odd thing on the Hunters?<br /> <br /> Peoples Guard MURDERS Nobles<br /> <br /> Magisters just send them into Coma's.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on Why I find it easier to picture any Noble I played Showing Forgiveness and Mercy to a member of the Peoples guard then a Magister<br /> <br /> or is it just me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the question. Who's more sympathetic in your eyes? A man who sees his kid daughter killed, then runs down the retreating killer and stabs him to death? Or a man who robs a bank, kills nobody, but is doing this just for material gain?<br /> <br /> It's because how they go about it and their mindsets. The People's Guard are hunters who unfortunately believe Nobles are the bad guys. In the case of Tears and Storms, it could well be justified for the People's Guard to step in and stop them. And up until the Release, most Nobles were Twilights, who genuinely did do a lot of damage - even if they had benevolent goals from their point of view. They don't understand the real difference between the Radiant and the Twilights. Many Radiant Nobles would probably rather spare them, sit them down, and talk - and try to get them on the same page. The essence of the conflict is tragic misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. Magisters know damn well what they're doing. They know that Nobles are doing their darnest to improve the world. Magisters kidnap and put Nobles in a coma simply because they think they can do better with the power, that it should be reallocated towards them. From the point of a view of a Noble, and probably a lot of people, Magisters are supremely arrogant. They hurt other people out of envy, so they can take their power.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. While the People's Guard hurt Nobles worse, their motives and mindset is a lot more sympathetic than the Magisters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri","name":"Tzauri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-19T18:38:58-08:00","id":1369075,"title":"","content":"Mirrors aren\u2019t that great either...<br /> <br /> I think Marie Antoinette would have made a great Princess of Mirrors.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25382\" data-vbnamecard=\"25382\">Tzauri</a> thanks for explaining the difference. The People\u2019s Guard sounds much more sympathetic than the Magisters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T16:21:08-08:00","id":1370174,"title":"","content":"On another Hunters Group? Star of Bethlahem is fascinating to me because it seems to be in a Transitional phase<br /> <br /> The compact seems likely to me to disband at some point when the impossiblety of their mission Dawns on them.<br /> <br /> That's at some point of course.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well Even if They find that taking on the Queens is Impossible or Ill advised, they'd probably just accept the bitter truth that sometime their is no once and for all over and done with solution.<br /> <br /> And still try to protect the children best they could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T18:27:33-08:00","id":1370202,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t remember them, but part of the Radiant Princesses\u2019 mission is to take care of the young ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T19:26:22-08:00","id":1370211,"title":"","content":"Stars of Bethlahem are a Hunter Compact who see the Queens as 'Conscripting' the Sensitives using them as child soldiers.<br /> <br /> They don't give a damn About the Difference between Twilight and Radiant.<br /> <br /> It seems to me they Probaly try (Fruitless) Efforts at applying conventional deprogramming techniques.to try dispelling Brainwashing That doesn't actually Exist.<br /> <br /> And probably look forward to an eventual reaction of tearful gratitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T20:26:59-08:00","id":1370220,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1153\" data-vbnamecard=\"1153\">Prince of the Night</a> A lot of these enemies confuse Radiant Princesses with Twilight Princesses. I had an idea for a character who Blossoms as a Princess of Mirrors when she\u2019s like 15 and then switches to Hearts when she\u2019s older and a little more mature. What do you (and anybody else) think of that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T07:03:34-08:00","id":1370343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340611-what-do-you-think-of-princess-the-hopeful?p=1370220#post1370220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1153\" data-vbnamecard=\"1153\">Prince of the Night</a> A lot of these enemies confuse Radiant Princesses with Twilight Princesses. I had an idea for a character who Blossoms as a Princess of Mirrors when she\u2019s like 15 and then switches to Hearts when she\u2019s older and a little more mature. What do you (and anybody else) think of that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally believable. Could be grounds for flashbacks or old emnimitys.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another Idea I had On Star of Bethlahem? How do you think they or other hunters Will react To seeing a Princess who narrowly Escapes becoming a Dethroned The other Sensitives are Panicked and in a rush talking with them.And then when they regain some degree of lucidity. Their immensely Relieved<br /> <br /> I Can picture the princesses tucking their Fellow into bed that night Reverently with love. When a few hours latter he has no pulse they cry but they are not paralyzed with Grief. And when the Stars find out this was the planned outcome I daren't guess what they'd think<br /> <br /> They might think a Coma is better as theyd probably Think eventually with their War on the Queens they could medicate away Tainted Shell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T07:36:32-08:00","id":1370351,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1153\" data-vbnamecard=\"1153\">Prince of the Night</a> why does she have no pulse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T07:58:43-08:00","id":1370358,"title":"","content":"Because she died peacefully in her Sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http